# Lumina - TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS

## 1. Authentication & Authorization (Auth & RBAC)

Uses Token-based authentication (e.g., JWT).

* **Registration/Login (Authentication):**
    * Supports standard login (Email/Password).
    * (Optional extension) SSO (Google/Microsoft).
* **Account Management:**
    * **Change Password:** Allows authenticated users to change their current password by providing the old password, a new password, and a password confirmation.
    * **Profile Management:** Users can view and edit their profile information, including name, email, and other details.
* **Localization & Internationalization (i18n):**
    * **System Interface Languages:** Supports multi-language switching across the entire platform interface. Supported languages: **Vietnamese, Japanese, and English**.
    * **User Preference:** Stores the user's selected language preference in their profile/local storage to persist across sessions.
* **Main System Roles & Scopes:**

    * **User (Normal User):**
        * Has CRUD rights for personal learning resources (Quiz, Document, Deck).
        * Resources created by a User **must be public**.
        * Can view other public resources but cannot edit resources not owned by them.
        * Can copy other public resources to create a personal version and has CRUD rights to this new version. This new version must also be public.
        * Can group resources (personal or public) into Collections.
        * Can join Organizations.
        * Can join Courses within an Organization when added by an Admin (can only access courses they have been added to).
        * Holds one of two roles within a Course: Teacher or Student.

    * **OrgAdmin (Organization Administrator):**
        * Management scope is restricted to a specific Organization.
        * Has the right to create Courses within that Organization.
        * Assign roles (Teacher/Student) to Users within a Course belonging to the Organization.
        * Manage Users within the Organization.
        * View Organization analytics/statistics.
        * Has full Teacher privileges in every course within that Organization.

    * **SysAdmin (System Administrator):**
        * Highest authority across the entire system.
        * Manage Organizations.
        * Manage Global Users.
        * Configure AI API Keys.
        * View global analytics/statistics.

## 2. Learning Resources Management (CRUD)

### 2.1. Quiz Management (AI-Powered)

* **Manual CRUD:** Manually create, edit, delete multiple-choice questions/answers. The Explanation field is not mandatory when creating manually.
* **AI Auto-Generation (Core Feature):**
    * **Input:** User uploads a PDF/Text file (Document object).
    * **Action:** Calls API (stepfun/step-3.5-flash) with a Prompt enforcing Zero Hallucination (only uses knowledge from the provided file).
    * **Language Matching:** The AI must generate the quiz elements (questions, options, explanations) in the same language as the uploaded source document.
    * **Output:** Returns strict JSON format (Question, Options, correct_index, Explanation). **The Explanation field is mandatory and must be based on the original document.**
    * **Verification:** Automatically parses JSON and saves it to the Database as a Draft Quiz. The User has the right to verify/edit before Publishing.

### 2.2. Document Management

* **Upload:** Supports uploading PDF files, images, and text files.
* **Storage:** Secure file storage (Database).
* **Viewer:** Integrated PDF/Image viewer directly on the LMS interface.

### 2.3. Flashcard Management

* **Card CRUD:** Create flashcards (Front: Keyword/Concept; Back: Definition/Description).
* **Deck CRUD:** Group Flashcards into Decks by topic.
* **Study Mode:**
    * Flashcard flipping mode for Users.
    * Supports the Shuffle function.
    * Allows Users to mark cards as "Mastered". The system will not display these cards in subsequent study sessions unless the User resets them.

### 2.4. Video Management (YouTube)

* **Upload Link:** Users provide YouTube links (no direct video file uploads to optimize storage resources).
* **Metadata:** Automatically extract video Title and Thumbnail from the YouTube API.
* **Embedded Viewer:** Integrated YouTube video player directly within the LMS.

## 3. Resource Grouping Mechanism (Module)

A Module is a general resource grouping mechanism that operates similarly to a Folder. Modules support nesting (a Module can contain other Modules).

### 3.1. Module Classification by Scope and Role

* **Collection (For Users):**
    * Created by Users to group learning resources (personal or public).
    * Has a public scope.

* **Course Module (For Teachers):**
    * Created by Teachers (or OrgAdmins with Teacher privileges) to group learning resources created within a course.
    * Scope is restricted to the course.

### 3.2. Module Structure

* **Module CRUD:** Create, edit, delete Modules (by Users for Collections; by Teachers/OrgAdmins for Course Modules).
* **Resource Items:**
    * Users can add/remove resources (Quiz, Document, Deck, Video link) to/from a Collection.
    * Teachers/OrgAdmins can add/remove resources (Quiz, Document, Deck, Video link) to/from a Course Module.
    * Supports custom ordering/sorting.

## 4. Course Management & Learning Functions

A Course belongs to an Organization. The OrgAdmin manages Course users and authorization.

### 4.1. Course Roles

* **Teacher:**
    * Has CRUD rights for learning resources within the course.
    * Has the right to create Modules to group resources within the course.
    * Can view the progress of Students in the course.

* **Student:**
    * Can only view (study) learning resources within the course.
    * The system records their viewing (study) progress in each course and updates the progress tracker.

### 4.2. Course Management (By OrgAdmin)

* **Course CRUD:** Create, edit, delete courses within the Organization.
* **User Management:** Add/remove Organization Users to/from courses.
* **Role Assignment:** Assign Teacher or Student roles to Users within a course.
* **Analytics:** View course statistics.

### 4.3. Learning Functions & Interaction (Student Flow in Course)

* **Participation:** Users join a Course when added by an Admin.
* **Study Flow:** Students study Items in a Module sequentially according to the learning path.
* **Progress Tracking:** The system automatically records and updates the Student's learning progress for each resource and course.
* **Doing Quiz:** Provides an interface for taking multiple-choice quizzes, including a timer and submission.
* **Grading:** Automatically grades the quiz. The Explanation is only displayed if it was provided. For AI-generated quizzes, the Explanation must be displayed since it is a mandatory field.